An elven wizard with an MM and with assistance from his cat had
just successfully cleared a leprechaun hall which was present a
couple of levels below the Oracle.  One of the leprechauns had a
scroll of create monster and had read it, creating a gargoyle, an
ettin zombie and a werejackal (and possibly others killed by the
cat).  These created a few problems for the wizard which required
repeated use of the E-word.  By the end of the clearance
operation both his HP and his Pw were pretty low.  The leprechaun
hall was a dead end so the wizard returned to the next room and
as he entered it, a monkey entered through one of the other
doors.  The monkey was checked to see if it was friendly or
hostile and on finding it to be hostile, the wizard threw a
dagger at it.  Next move, the monkey appears to have turned into
a mastodon; no messages indicating death of the monkey.  Wizard
backs away, into corridor with intention of using remaining Pw to
fire an MM at the mastodon.  MM has no effect on the creature and
the wizard is butted by the mastodon and dies.

So the question is: where did that mastodon come from?  There
wasn't a poly trap in the room.  I presume that it wasn't a
chameleon as I understand that they use their own attack formula
regardless of their visual form; am I correct in this belief?

The only possibility that I can think of is that the monkey
retreated at the same time as the mastodon entered the room but
at the time, the timing seemed wrong for that and there was no
message saying that the monkey was fleeing.

